{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The New Roads Ahead", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Either Today or Tomorrow ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 7, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information involving apologies, thanks, suggestions and invitations in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Describes events that happened at work, using appropriate expressions and well-constructed simple past phrases.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Describes events that happened at work, using appropriate expressions and well-constructed simple past phrases.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Intonation and Prominence  ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Intonation</span> <br><span class=\"strong\">Intonation: </span>The rise and fall of your tone of voice when you speak.  Wh- questions end in a falling tone. Yes/No questions end in a rising tone.<br>The meaning of what you say depends on the tone or pitch of your voice.  <br><br> <span class=\"underline\">Prominence</span> <br><span class=\"strong\">Prominence:</span> The emphasis you put on a word in a phrase or sentence to show that it is important.  It is usually the last content word in a short sentence.<br>A syllable can be made prominent using loudness, pitch and length.<br><br>In the examples, words with rising intonation have CAPITAL letters. Words with prominence have <span class=\"strong\">CAPITAL AND BOLD</span> letters.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " Peter WALKED in the<span class=\"strong\"> DARK</span>.      ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Sally SAT in the LAST <span class=\"strong\">ROW</span>.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Which CREDit CARD <span class=\"strong\">COM</span>panies CHARGE an ANNual <span class=\"strong\">FEE</span>?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you plan to meet someone.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "reservation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a booking or an appointment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Shall I make a reservation at Mineo's?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "long time no see", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an expression used when you meet someone you have not seen in a long time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Long time no see. What have you been up to?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to catch up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to meet someone to talk about their life", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How about we meet up for pizza to catch up?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Hawaiian", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a kind of pizza with pineapple and ham", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Is Hawaiian pizza still your favorite?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "either", "type": "name"}, {"content": "introduces a choice between two things - either/or", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(conjunction)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Are you free either today or tomorrow?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to make it", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to change it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Can you make it 7:00 p.m.?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Make a list of five people you want to go to dinner with.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What questions do you want to ask them about their lives? Example: <span class=\"italic\">What do you like for dessert?</span> Use a word with the <span class=\"italic\">er</span> sound in each question like <span class=\"italic\">mother</span>, <span class=\"italic\">brother</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">spider</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use rising intonation if it is a yes/no question. Use falling intonation it is a <span class=\"italic\">Wh-</span> question.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write the five questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read each question aloud.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I make a list of people I want to have dinner with.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask questions about people's lives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write questions that use words with the <span class=\"italic\">er</span> sound.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn3le07ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn3le07ob04re2img02.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn3le07ob04re2img02.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn3le07ob04re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Hey Peter. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Hi Sally. How are you?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Great! Long time no see. What have you been up to?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I've been busy at work.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Oh ... internships are hard. There is so much to learn.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Yes ... So many e-mails and reports. Argh!<br>", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn3le07ob04re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: How about we meet up for pizza to catch up?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: When?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Either today or tomorrow. Are you free?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I'm going to a friend's birthday dinner tonight. Tomorrow?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span> : No problem. Shall I make a reservation at Mineo's? At 6:30?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Can you make it 7:00 p.m.? I have to write a 1,000 word report first.<br>", "time": "21000", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn3le07ob04re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Sure. I'll be there a little early. I'll order us some drinks and garlic bread. Is Hawaiian still your favorite?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Absolutely! See ya tomorrow.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Ciao.<br>", "time": "44500", "id": 3}]}}], "id": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can say and use the controlled vowel sound <span class=\"italic\">er</span>.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can say simple statements.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can identify key information in a short audio.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Where do you \u2018catch up' with friends? At the park? A restaurant?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Are you good at keeping in touch with your friends? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partne